# Prefer the web Settings > AI configuration form for everyday changes.
# Copy to backend/.env.local for optional fallback configuration.
# Saved web AI settings take precedence over AI environment/local-file values.
# Restore environment configuration in the web form to remove that override.
# Environment variables take precedence over this file. Never commit credentials.
# Leave AI_API_KEY empty to run the dashboard without fresh AI generation.
AI_PROVIDER=anthropic
AI_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides; blank values use the backend's Anthropic defaults.
AI_API_URL=
AI_MODEL=

# For an OpenAI-compatible service, replace the settings above with:
# AI_PROVIDER=openai_compatible
# AI_API_KEY=
# AI_API_URL=https://your-provider.example/v1/chat/completions
# AI_MODEL=your-provider-model
# Supply the service root, a /v1 base, or the full chat-completions endpoint.
# The adapter normalizes these forms without duplicating /v1.
# Supported provider names: anthropic, openai, openai_compatible,
# dashscope_anthropic, kimi.

# Optional generation/cache tuning (provider-specific timeout noted below):
# AI_TEMPERATURE=0.2
# AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=1400
# AI_CACHE_LIMIT=20
# AI_HTTP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# The timeout defaults to 30 seconds for Anthropic, 120 for OpenAI-compatible
# services, and 300 for DashScope/Kimi when no override is supplied.

# The default database is investment_board.db in the project root.
# To change it when using scripts/run_all.sh or scripts/run_backend.sh,
# export DATABASE_URL in your shell before launching; the scripts set it.
# Example: export DATABASE_URL="sqlite:////absolute/path/to/demo.db"
# When starting uvicorn directly, DATABASE_URL can also be set in this file.
